# State management

## Roles

| Kind | Where / tool |
|------|----------------|
| **Document + canvas model** (pages, nodes, undo-related coordination) | **`src/features/editor/stores/docStore.ts`** (+ Immer), **history** in **`core/history/**` |
| **Tool / UI modes** (selection, pan, marquee, overlays) | **`src/features/editor/stores/**`** (e.g. `toolStore`, `selectionStore`, …) |
| **Future remote/server lists** | **TanStack Query** under **`src/hooks/query/**`** |
| **Local-only UI** | **`useState` / `useReducer`** in the smallest subtree |

## Zustand (editor) — Do

- Keep stores **typed** and **small actions**; use **`getState()`** only outside React when the codebase already does (e.g. shortcuts, bridges).
- Select minimal slices in components to avoid useless re-renders.

## Zustand — Don’t

- Don’t duplicate **full document/server payloads** in new global stores — **`doc`** stays authoritative in **`docStore`** + persistence via **`docsService`**.
- Don’t persist **tokens/passwords** in Zustand.

## TanStack Query

- When backend APIs arrive: **server lists/details** live in Query; editor canvas state stays in editor stores unless you’re explicitly syncing.

## Security

- Follow **`000-core.mdc`**. DevTools can inspect client stores — no secrets in plain fields.
